member.summary:
Entry point of the store engine for credential handling. Implementations talk to App Store Connect and Google Play;
tests use a fake. The secret is the JSON the user pasted: for Apple {"issuerId","keyId","privateKey"}, for
Google the service account key file as downloaded.

What a handler sees of its job and how it reports progress. Every step call renews the job's lease, publishes a live
event and, at most about once a second, checks whether a member cancelled the job (then it throws
).

HMAC-SHA256 webhook signatures. App Store Connect signs the raw body and sends x-apple-signature: hmacsha256=<hex>;
storeasy's own scheme (inbound signed webhooks and outgoing deliveries) signs {timestamp}.{body} and sends
X-Storeasy-Signature: sha256=<hex> with X-Storeasy-Timestamp (unix seconds). Comparisons are constant time.
